  "summary": "Five papers dated 2026-11-06 benchmark DIA search tools, quantitation utilities and postprocessing across spike-in, plasma and cardiovascular datasets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluating DIA proteomics at the workflow level rather than ranking single search engines. One study crosses four search tools (DIA-NN, DIA-Umpire, diaTracer, MSFragger-DIA) with four quantitation utilities on two spike-in datasets. Another uses controlled human/yeast/bacterial mixtures on two MS platforms to benchmark DIA-NN postprocessing and derive quantification recommendations. A ZenoTOF plasma benchmark with DIA-NN and Spectronaut found DIA-NN library mode detected true changes best. A cardiovascular study compares three DDA and five DIA tools on real tissue and blood data. The Manchester Proteome Profiler, an open-source R Shiny app, addresses downstream filtering, normalization, imputation, differential expression, clustering and enrichment. Together the papers pair controlled ground truth with real-sample evaluation.",
